# The same HPM.1 image with a corrupted signature. Because the MD5 is computed
# over the corrupted bytes the image is still self-consistent, so the failure
# ipmitool reports is specifically "Invalid image signature".

@mark image
@mark header
50 49 43 4d 47 46 57 58   # "PICMGFWX" - last byte wrong
00
20
57 01 00
01 00
00 e1 0b 5e
08
01
05
05
05
00 02
01 00 00 00 00 00
00 00
@mark hdrsum
00
@fill_checksum hdrsum header
@mark a1
01
01
@mark a1sum
00
@fill_checksum a1sum a1
@md5 image
